  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "There exists an infinitely large two-dimensional grid of uncolored unit cells. You receive a positive integer `n`, indicating that you must do the following routine for `n` minutes:\n\n* At the first minute, color **any** arbitrary unit cell blue.\n* Every minute thereafter, color blue **every** uncolored cell that touches a blue cell.\n\nBelow is a pictorial representation of the state of the grid after minutes 1, 2, and 3.\n\n![](https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2023/01/10/example-copy-2.png)\n\nOutput *the number of **colored cells** at the end of* `n` *minutes*.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: n = 1\nOutput: 1\nExplanation: After 1 minute, there is only 1 blue cell, so we return 1.\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: n = 2\nOutput: 5\nExplanation: After 2 minutes, there are 4 colored cells on the boundary and 1 in the center, so we return 5.\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= n <= 105`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
